# Low Water, Act 2: The Weigh-house on Night 2 (prefix weigh2.). Writer's draft, 2026-10-17. Private.
# Places (Act 1 records): weigh_out, weigh_in (the switch room, behind the Trust's new partition),
# tube, roof. What it holds (ACT2-RETURNING): the Trust holds the switch room; the tube thumps at
# 04:00 (ev2.tube_thump); from 05:30 the town gathers here for the dawn meeting about the gale, and
# the night ends in this file (dawn2.start at 06:02, by the event or the last option).
# The gate this file owns: the switch room, five routes (Fist e.switchroom, Tongue, Shadow the roof,
# Hands the padlocked handle, Eye the card through the window).
# Reads from Act 1: cause.*, book.violence, seenas_trust, tab_hobb, weigh.roof_ok, mother, var.lens,
# frost.met, merrow.cells, seenas_guild, lamp.balance.lit, day.pip. From Act 2: fisk.button,
# i.fisk_spec, a2.masters, a2.relics, met.fisk.

# ---- new ids
@fact weigh2.in

@fact weigh2.feeder

@fact weigh2.fetched_wenna

@fact weigh2.tube_read

@fact weigh2.pulled

@fact weigh2.followed_pipe

@fact down.weigh2
@fact weigh2.door_held

@fact weigh2.board_card
about: On the quay board, a card in yellow ink: HEAD LIGHT TO REMAIN ON QUAY BOARD. NOT TO BE RESTORED TO OWN FEEDER WITHOUT THE ALDERMAN. O.C. Dated this morning.
against: trust 15
by: reading, out of the sodium

@fact weigh2.log_delay
about: The Lamplighters' board log for Low Night: 02:50, board drowned. 02:51, Alderman by telephone: no hurry. 03:20, reset.
against: trust 10
by: reading

@fact weigh2.ink_wet
about: The Shelf's four o'clock strip came down the tube with its ink still wet.
by: the Damp

@encounter e.switchroom
name: The Trust's switch room
area: weigh
foe: f.guard 2
param: white-light (the guards' lanterns are Municipal white)
win: weigh2.fight.room.win
yield: weigh2.fight.room.yield
fled: weigh2.fight.room.fled
down: weigh2.fight.room.down

talk: weigh2.fx.card | Read them the card over the board ? fight_seconds >= 8
talk: weigh2.fx.gorm | Ask whether the sergeant knows what they're guarding ? (fight_struck >= 1 | fight_seconds >= 10)

@node weigh2.fx.card
place: weigh_in
speaker: STRAND
cost: 2
line: LAMB: "Not to be restored to her own feeder without the Alderman." That's what you're standing on. Mother's off her own wire so the Alderman can keep a hand on her, and you two are the hand.
line: STRAND: Coe. Put it down.
line: COE: I've written it. I'm putting it down.
go: weigh2.fight.room.yield

@node weigh2.fx.gorm
place: weigh_in
speaker: STRAND
cost: 2
line: LAMB: Does the sergeant know what's on that card? Ask her. Ask her about the telephone at nine minutes to three last night.
line: STRAND: The sergeant knows what she's told.
line: COE: Strand. She asked me what the log said. This morning. Twice.
nar: Strand grounds her pole.
go: weigh2.fight.room.yield

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the hub
@node weigh2.hub
place: weigh_out
hub: yes
cost: 0
alt: weigh2.arrive ? !seen(weigh2.arrive)
alt: weigh2.tube.thump ? clock >= 04:00 & clock < 04:20 & !seen(weigh2.tube.thump)
alt: weigh2.gather ? clock >= 05:30 & !seen(weigh2.gather)
nar: The weigh-house under a clear sky, frost on the brick, a white lantern in the window.
nar: Up on the balance, last night's small yellow flame. {when: has(lamp.balance.lit)}
nar: Sea smoke off the harbour. The town is arriving. {when: clock >= 05:30}
opt: "Go to the switch-room door." -> weigh2.door ? !has(weigh2.in) +1
opt: "Go back into the switch room." -> weigh2.room ? has(weigh2.in) +1
opt: "Look in at the switch-room window." -> weigh2.window ? !has(weigh2.board_card) +1 {verb: hide, noise: 0.1}
opt: "Look at the switch box under the eave." -> weigh2.box +1
check: "[GRIP] Climb to the balance and lift the slates over the board." -> weigh2.roof.ok / weigh2.roof.fail ? !has(weigh2.in) & !has(weigh.roof_ok) {skill: grip, dc: 6, verb: climb, noise: 0.3}
opt: "Climb to the balance, the way you know, and lift the slates over the board." -> weigh2.roof.ok ? !has(weigh2.in) & has(weigh.roof_ok) {verb: climb, noise: 0.2}
opt: "Go through to the tube room." -> weigh2.tube +1
opt: "Go back to the quay." -> quay2.hub +1
opt: "Cut through to the Gut." -> gut2.hub +2

@node weigh2.arrive
place: weigh_out
speaker: STRAND
cost: 2
nar: A new partition across the after-vote hall, a locked door in it, and two Lamplighters with white lanterns: Strand, and Coe, who writes everything twice.
nar: On the outer door, printed: BY ORDER. THE QUAY SWITCH IS MUNICIPAL PROPERTY. THE GUILD'S VOTE IS SUSPENDED PENDING REVIEW. {when: has(cause.guild)}
nar: Two more poles lean by the door. {when: has(book.violence)}
line: STRAND: Evening, assessor. Municipal. You'll want to keep walking.
line: COE: Assessor, evening, nineteen-twelve. Written.
line: STRAND: The Trust's guarding its own board against your verdict, if you're wondering. It's very good at that. {when: has(cause.trust) & !has(cause.guild)}
go: weigh2.hub

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the switch room: the gate (five routes)
@node weigh2.door
place: weigh_in
speaker: STRAND
cost: 2
line: STRAND: Nobody past. The Alderman's own instruction, in her own ink.
line: COE: Nobody past. I've written it on the door as well, in case.
opt: "Let me past." -> weigh2.door.relief ? guise == lamplighter {verb: hide, noise: 0.1}
opt: "Hobb, let me through." -> weigh2.door.hobb ? var.tab_hobb == 1
check: "[FORM LETTER] The insurer inspects the insured's equipment. Now, please." -> weigh2.door.talk.ok / weigh2.door.talk.fail ? !seen(weigh2.door.talk.fail) {skill: formletter, dc: 7}
opt: "Go through them." -> weigh2.door.fight ? !has(down.weigh2) & !has(weigh2.door_held) {verb: pry, noise: 0.9}
opt: "Leave them to their door." -> weigh2.hub

@node weigh2.door.relief
place: weigh_in
speaker: COE
cost: 2
do: set(weigh2.in); set(book.weigh2_guise)
line: COE: You're early. I've written you early. Key's on the nail inside.
nar: He looks at the dark coat and nowhere else.
go: weigh2.room

@node weigh2.door.hobb
place: weigh_in
speaker: HOBB
cost: 3
do: set(weigh2.in); tab_hobb = 0; set(book.weigh2_hobb)
line: HOBB: Strand. Sergeant wants you both at the step. Something about a cart. I'll mind the door.
nar: Strand and Coe go. Hobb opens the partition with his eyes on the floor.
line: HOBB: That's us square, Shelf. I'll be on nights in the cells after this. I don't mind the cells. They've a lamp.
go: weigh2.room

@node weigh2.door.talk.ok
place: weigh_in
speaker: STRAND
cost: 3
do: set(weigh2.in); set(said.inspect2); set(book.inspect2)
line: LAMB: That board carries an insured light. The insurer inspects the insured's equipment on demand. Refusal goes in my report, and the Alderman reads my report aloud to the Board.
line: STRAND: Five minutes. Coe watches you.
line: COE: I write what you touch.
go: weigh2.room

@node weigh2.door.talk.fail
place: weigh_in
speaker: COE
cost: 2
do: set(book.inspect2_refused)
line: COE: The Shelf's paper isn't honoured at the Municipal. That came down from the hill at six. I've written that you asked. Twice.
go: weigh2.hub

@node weigh2.door.fight
place: weigh_in
speaker: STRAND
cost: 1
do: rep(trust, -1); set(book.violence)
line: STRAND: Coe. Book away.
nar: Coe closes his book, which is how the assessor knows he means it.
alt: weigh2.door.fight.fallback ? var.runs == 0 | !runs
do: fight(e.switchroom)

@node weigh2.door.fight.fallback
place: weigh_in
cost: 3
check: "[GRIP] Take Strand's pole by the brass and turn her on it." -> weigh2.fight.room.win / weigh2.fight.room.down {skill: grip, dc: 7}
check: "[FORM LETTER] Read them the card over the board, through the open door." -> weigh2.fx.card / weigh2.fight.room.down ? has(weigh2.board_card) {skill: formletter, dc: 6}
opt: "Hands up. You yield." -> weigh2.fight.room.yield
opt: "Back out of the door into the frost." -> weigh2.fight.room.fled

@node weigh2.fight.room.win
place: weigh_in
speaker: STRAND
cost: 3
do: set(weigh2.in); set(weigh2.board_card)
if: trait(m.body) == none => offer(m.body)
if: trait(m.poles) == none => offer(m.poles)
nar: Coe is under the trestle after his pencil. Over the board, a card in yellow ink: HEAD LIGHT TO REMAIN ON QUAY BOARD. NOT TO BE RESTORED TO OWN FEEDER WITHOUT THE ALDERMAN. O.C.
line: STRAND: Go on, then. It's not as if we could stop you writing it down.
go: weigh2.room

@node weigh2.fight.room.yield
place: weigh_in
speaker: STRAND
cost: 2
line: STRAND: That's enough of that. You've been told no, assessor, and now you've been shown it.
do: set(weigh2.door_held)
nar: They walk the Shelf to the outer door and leave it on the step, and a third lantern comes to stand with them.
go: weigh2.hub

@node weigh2.fight.room.fled
place: weigh_out
speaker: COE
cost: 2
do: meter(dread, 1)
do: set(weigh2.door_held)
line: COE: Assessor, departing, at speed. Written.
go: weigh2.hub

@node weigh2.fight.room.down
place: weigh_out
speaker: HOBB
cost: 30
do: set(down.weigh2); meter(cold, 2)
nar: The step, the frost, and Hobb's spare lantern lit beside the assessor's head.
line: HOBB: They've gone for the sergeant. The slates are loose over the board, Shelf. By the balance post. I only say it because they are.
go: weigh2.hub

# Shadow: through the roof by the balance
@node weigh2.roof.ok
place: roof
cost: 4
nar: By the balance post three slates lift. Below, a lit well: the board, the lantern, two heads facing the wrong way.
check: "[THE DARK] Lower yourself down the post between their backs." -> weigh2.drop.ok / weigh2.drop.fail {skill: dark, dc: 6, verb: hide, noise: 0.3}
opt: "Put the slates back and climb down." -> weigh2.hub

@node weigh2.roof.fail
place: weigh_out
speaker: COE
cost: 3
do: wet(0.2); meter(cold, 1)
nar: The drainpipe is frozen. Halfway up, the hands lose the argument.
line: COE: Somebody fell off the weigh-house. Writing it.
go: weigh2.hub

@node weigh2.drop.ok
place: weigh_in
speaker: STRAND
cost: 3
do: set(weigh2.in)
nar: Down the post into the warm air.
line: STRAND: My feet have stopped, Coe. Both of them.
line: COE: I'll write it.
nar: Neither turns round.
go: weigh2.room

@node weigh2.drop.fail
place: weigh_in
speaker: COE
cost: 3
do: set(book.weigh2_roof)
nar: A slate slides and stops half over the edge. Coe's lantern comes up into the roof.
line: COE: Strand. There's a Shelf in the roof.
line: STRAND: Then it can come down the front like a Christian. Down the front, please, assessor.
go: weigh2.hub

# Hands: the padlocked handle
@node weigh2.box
place: weigh_out
cost: 1
nar: A new Municipal padlock hangs on the switch handle so it cannot come down.
check: "[GRIP] Work the padlock's hasp off with the Vane's stick, and pull the quay switch." -> weigh2.box.ok / weigh2.box.fail ? power.quay == on & !has(weigh2.pulled) {skill: grip, dc: 6, verb: cutpower, noise: 0.6}
opt: "Leave it." -> weigh2.hub

@node weigh2.box.ok
place: weigh_in
speaker: STRAND
cost: 4
do: set(weigh2.pulled); set(weigh2.in); set(book.weigh2_switch); rep(trust, -1)
if: mother == burning & !has(weigh2.feeder) => set(mother.out_again)
cmd: setPower quay off
nar: The hasp gives, the handle comes down, and Lamp Quay goes out under the stars.
line: STRAND: Coe! The quay!
nar: They run out with their lanterns high. The assessor goes in by the door they left open.
nar: At the end of the mole, Mother's beam goes out. {when: has(mother.out_again)}
go: weigh2.room

@node weigh2.box.fail
place: weigh_out
speaker: STRAND
cost: 2
do: set(book.weigh2_box)
nar: The stick slips off the hasp with a clang the length of the quay. The door opens.
line: STRAND: That's Municipal brass, assessor. Leave it be, or I'll leave you be in the cells.
go: weigh2.hub

# Eye: the card through the window
@node weigh2.window
place: weigh_out
cost: 3
nar: Through the glass: the board, a white lantern, and over the main switch a card that, under the quay's sodium, has nothing written on it.
check: "[SMALL PRINT] Wait for Coe to open the stove door, and read the card by its glow." -> weigh2.window.ok / weigh2.window.fail {skill: smallprint, dc: 7, verb: wait, noise: 0}
opt: "Leave the window." -> weigh2.hub

@node weigh2.window.ok
place: weigh_out
cost: 6
do: set(weigh2.board_card)
nar: Coe opens the stove. For a moment the blank card has yellow writing on it: HEAD LIGHT TO REMAIN ON QUAY BOARD. NOT TO BE RESTORED TO OWN FEEDER WITHOUT THE ALDERMAN. O.C.
go: weigh2.hub

@node weigh2.window.fail
place: weigh_out
cost: 5
do: journal("Pencil: the card on the quay board says HEAD LIGHT TO BE RESTORED. The Trust means to put her back. Check.")
nar: The stove flares, and the assessor reads, through glass and frost, what a tired assessor hopes to read. It goes in pencil.
go: weigh2.hub

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- inside the switch room
@node weigh2.room
place: weigh_in
cost: 1
nar: The quay board: a slate face as big as a door, knife switches, and two new brass links joining HEAD LIGHT to QUAY.
opt: "Read the card over the main switch." -> weigh2.card ? !has(weigh2.board_card) {verb: read}
opt: "Read the board log on its nail." -> weigh2.log ? !has(weigh2.log_delay) {verb: read}
opt: "Unbolt the two brass links and give Mother back her own feeder." -> weigh2.feeder.fisk ? !has(weigh2.feeder) & (has(fisk.button) | count(i.fisk_spec) > 0) {verb: rig, noise: 0.4}
check: "[GRIP] Unbolt the two brass links and give Mother back her own feeder." -> weigh2.feeder.ok / weigh2.feeder.fail ? !has(weigh2.feeder) & !has(fisk.button) & count(i.fisk_spec) == 0 {skill: grip, dc: 7, verb: rig, noise: 0.4}
opt: "Leave." -> weigh2.hub

@node weigh2.card
place: weigh_in
cost: 2
do: set(weigh2.board_card)
nar: HEAD LIGHT TO REMAIN ON QUAY BOARD. NOT TO BE RESTORED TO OWN FEEDER WITHOUT THE ALDERMAN. O.C. Dated this morning, in the hand that struck the clause.
go: weigh2.room

@node weigh2.log
place: weigh_in
cost: 2
do: set(weigh2.log_delay)
nar: The board log, a school exercise book on a nail. Low Night, in Hobb's round hand: 02:50, board drowned, rain. 02:51, ALDERMAN BY TELEPHONE: NO HURRY. 03:20, reset.
voice: sum: Thirty minutes of dark, twenty-nine of them by instruction. {dc: 6}
go: weigh2.room

@node weigh2.feeder.fisk
place: weigh_in
cost: 5
do: set(weigh2.feeder); rep(trust, -1); set(book.feeder)
nar: Fisk's drawing shows the four bolts, drawn by a man who expected someone to need them undone. The links come off warm, and HEAD LIGHT drops back onto its own feeder with a small dry click.
go: weigh2.room

@node weigh2.feeder.ok
place: weigh_in
cost: 6
do: set(weigh2.feeder); rep(trust, -1); set(book.feeder)
nar: Four frozen bolts and a Shelf penknife. The last gives like a knuckle. HEAD LIGHT drops back onto its own feeder with a small dry click.
go: weigh2.room

@node weigh2.feeder.fail
place: weigh_in
cost: 4
do: set(book.feeder); rep(trust, -1); meter(cold, 1)
cmd: setPower quay off
nar: The penknife slips across the main. The quay blinks pink, and every face on it turns to the window where the Shelf stands at the Trust's board with a knife.
cmd: setPower quay on
go: weigh2.hub

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the tube, and the four o'clock thump
@node weigh2.pip.turn
place: tube
speaker: PIP
cost: 6
do: set(quay2.move_turn); rep(shelf, 1)
line: PIP: You don't get past. You let them come at you, and when they lean, you turn on the ball of the foot, and you're behind them, and they're still leaning.
line: PIP: Grandad taught me on the quay with a broom. He was the broom.
nar: She shows it in the tube room, twice, round the assessor, and the second time the assessor feels nothing go by at all.
voice: knees: The ball of the foot. Not the heel. Never the heel on frost. {dc: 4}
go: weigh2.tube

@node weigh2.tube
place: tube
cost: 1
alt: weigh2.tube.later ? clock >= 04:20 & !has(weigh2.tube_read)
nar: The tube room, the brass mouth frosted round its rim, the basket empty.
nar: Under Pip's card, in another hand: AND HER GRANDMOTHER. {when: has(day.pip)}
opt: "Put your ear to the brass." -> weigh2.tube.ear ? !seen(weigh2.tube.ear) {verb: eavesdrop, noise: 0}
check: "[THE DAMP] Follow the pipe out of the wall by the frost along its line." -> weigh2.pipe.ok / weigh2.pipe.fail ? clock >= 01:00 {skill: damp, dc: 3, verb: read, noise: 0.1}
opt: "Ask Pip how she gets past the Lamplighters with the canister." -> weigh2.pip.turn ? !has(quay2.move_turn)
opt: "Go back out." -> weigh2.hub

@node weigh2.tube.ear
place: tube
cost: 2
nar: A long dry breath, very far up. Then, once, a cough: small, old, and nearer than the Shelf has any right to be.
go: weigh2.tube

@node weigh2.pipe.ok
place: tube
cost: 3
nar: Where the pipe goes under the cobbles the frost has not settled: a dark stripe the width of a hand, up the quay toward the Ropewalk.
inst: THE DAMP: Warm air in the pipe, all night. A fire at the other end.
opt: "Follow the stripe." -> ropewalk.hub +6 {verb: wait, noise: 0.1, do: set(weigh2.followed_pipe)}
opt: "Not yet." -> weigh2.hub

@node weigh2.pipe.fail
place: tube
cost: 2
inst: THE DAMP: Frost. Everywhere frost. I am a hair. Ask a dog.
go: weigh2.tube

@node weigh2.tube.thump
place: tube
speaker: PIP
cost: 3
do: set(weigh2.tube_read); quest(a2.typist, heard)
nar: At four the brass mouth coughs. Pip unscrews the canister with numb fingers and holds the strip to the lamp. Every e sits half a line high.
line: PIP: SHELF TO ASSESSOR LAMB. GALE FORECAST FROM HESK FOR TONIGHT. THE TOWN WILL MEET AT SIX. THE SHELF WILL ATTEND.
line: PIP: It's never said that. Attend. It's never been anywhere.
check: "[THE DAMP] Lay the Damp across the ink." -> weigh2.ink.ok / weigh2.ink.fail ? var.damp_wet != 1 {skill: damp, dc: 3, verb: read, noise: 0}
opt: "Fold it into the Daybook." -> weigh2.hub

@node weigh2.ink.ok
place: tube
cost: 1
do: set(weigh2.ink_wet)
inst: THE DAMP: Wet. Wet as a lip. Five minutes, not more, since a ribbon touched this.
go: weigh2.hub

@node weigh2.ink.fail
place: tube
cost: 1
inst: THE DAMP: The paper is cold and the air is colder and I cannot tell you which of them is lying.
go: weigh2.hub

@node weigh2.tube.later
place: tube
cost: 2
do: set(weigh2.tube_read)
nar: Rolled in the basket where Pip left it: SHELF TO ASSESSOR LAMB. GALE FORECAST FROM HESK FOR TONIGHT. THE TOWN WILL MEET AT SIX. THE SHELF WILL ATTEND. Every e half a line high.
go: weigh2.tube

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- 05:30: the town gathers (beat 16)
@node weigh2.gather
place: weigh_in
cost: 6
nar: Sea smoke comes in at the door at knee height, and the town arrives wading in it. The partition stands open.
line: MARROW: Gale, the Glass says. Then we'll need a light, won't we, and not the Trust's. {when: var.seenas_guild != "informer"}
line: SPRATT: The steward's not coming. I'm in his chair. Get used to it. {when: var.seenas_guild == "informer"}
line: KEEL: The Board is present. The Board is always present. {when: !has(frost.met) | var.lens != "broken"}
nar: The harbourmaster stands with his hat in his hands. There is glass in the seams of his coat. {when: has(frost.met) & var.lens == "broken"}
line: SABINE: She's not coming, and I'll not tell you twice what it costs to ask her. {when: has(cause.keeper)}
line: WENNA: I'll sit. Somebody give me the trestle. {when: !has(cause.keeper)}
line: LUGG: Tub's behind a grating. I'm the Low Company tonight. {when: has(merrow.cells)}
line: MERROW: Gale by dark. I'll stand by the door. {when: !has(merrow.cells)}
line: PENHALLOW: Three logs, assessor. Thirty-one nights of green between them. {when: quest(a2.masters) == signed}
line: FISK: I have the specification, if anyone, at any point, wishes to see it. {when: has(met.fisk)}
line: FENNICK: We have come to listen, assessor. Only to listen. {when: quest(a2.relics) != counted}
line: GAUZE: The deacon sends his regrets. I'm to hear everything twice. {when: quest(a2.relics) == counted}
line: GORM: And would the Shelf like to know that the Alderman is not coming? And that she has sent a letter? And that I am not to open it until six?
line: PIP: Four o'clock strip, assessor. I kept it dry. {when: has(weigh2.tube_read)}
opt: "Go and fetch Wenna from the Brine." -> weigh2.fetch ? has(cause.keeper) & clock < 05:50 {verb: carry, noise: 0.2}
opt: "Take a place by the pans and wait for six." -> dawn2.start

@node weigh2.fetch
place: brine
speaker: WENNA
cost: 10
nar: Wenna by the cold stove with her coat on.
line: WENNA: You put me up the tube. Now you want me in a room with them.
check: "[CONDOLENCE] Tell her the gale does not care whose fault the lamp is." -> weigh2.fetch.ok / weigh2.fetch.fail {skill: condolence, dc: 7}
opt: "Leave her." -> weigh2.gather.back

@node weigh2.fetch.ok
place: weigh_in
speaker: WENNA
cost: 8
do: set(weigh2.fetched_wenna)
line: WENNA: She doesn't. She's the only one in Gullet who doesn't.
nar: They walk back in the sea smoke. The weigh-house goes quiet when she comes in, and Sabine moves along the trestle to make room.
opt: "Take a place by the pans and wait for six." -> dawn2.start

@node weigh2.fetch.fail
place: brine
speaker: WENNA
cost: 2
line: WENNA: Go and stand in your room, assessor. I've a lamp to think about.
go: weigh2.gather.back

@node weigh2.gather.back
place: weigh_in
speaker: MARROW
cost: 8
line: MARROW: Kept your place by the pans, Shelf. Nobody's decided about you yet.
opt: "Take the place and wait for six." -> dawn2.start
